=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a runner's name inside another word does not make a runner site
origin: issue #196 ruling 191.5 — runner names count as whole words, so `jest` in `deploy-majestic.sh`
origin2: is no runner. v0.5.0 blocked this diff as "./deploy-majestic.sh is disabled".
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
      - run: ./deploy-majestic.sh
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
      - run: ./deploy-majestic.sh
        if: github.event_name == 'push'
